# Normalise text to LF in the repository.
#
# History: this repo was authored on Windows with core.autocrlf unset and no
# .gitattributes. A later checkout wrote CRLF into the working tree while the
# committed blobs stayed LF, so `git status` reported all 566 text files as
# modified indefinitely. The content was byte-identical apart from the CR --
# verified with `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` (empty) and by hashing every
# binary against HEAD. The working tree was restored rather than renormalised,
# so no commit rewrites 2015 content. This file stops it recurring.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never touch these.
*.rda    binary
*.RData  binary
*.rdb    binary
*.rdx    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.svg    binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.xls    binary
*.zip    binary
*.doc    binary
*.docx   binary

# Vendored source data is a byte-exact mirror of the 2015 raw tree. Git must
# never transform it -- checksums in vendor/README.md are the proof of fidelity.
vendor/** -text
